{
 "id": "11-s11-not-a-picture",
 "text": "Here's something easy to forget. Understanding the world isn't only about knowing what things look like. A familiar voice tells you who's nearby. Footsteps reveal that someone is approaching. Touch gives you details that sound alone cannot. And memory helps you understand places you've learned. Blind people use many different combinations of senses, skills and tools. Echolocation is one remarkable possibility among them. The goal isn't to recreate eyesight. It's to gain useful information and greater independence.",
 "seconds": 33.91,
 "source": "tts-with-timestamps",
